TITLE:: JMDrawIcons
summary:: Extra icons for the wslib Quark
categories:: GUI>Views, Libraries>jostMlib
related::  Classes/UserView

DESCRIPTION::
Adds some nice icons to wslib's DrawIcon collection
Checks if wslib is preset. You can still use the draw functions independently with getFuncs.at(\key);
Can be used WITHOUT wslib too. see below.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: initClass

METHOD:: getFuncs
gets all of the draw function

returns:: an Event (\key1: func, \key2: func)

METHOD:: listKeys
lists all the functions
EXAMPLES::

code::
// Use WITH wslib Quark
(
JMDrawIcons.listKeys;
FlowView.new(nil, Window.flipY(Rect(300,300,350,600))).flow{|w|
    JMDrawIcons.getFuncs.order.do{|key,i|
		StaticText(w,Rect(0,0,70,50)).string_("\\"++key.asString);
        RoundButton(w,50@40).states_([[key]]).radius_(0);
        (i%2).booleanValue.if{ w.startRow;};
    };
}
)

// Use WITHOUT wslib Quark

(
JMDrawIcons.listKeys;
FlowView.new(nil, Window.flipY(Rect(300,300,350,600))).flow{|w|
    JMDrawIcons.getFuncs.keysValuesDo{|key,val,i|
    	StaticText(w,Rect(0,0,70,50)).string_("\\"++key.asString);
        UserView(w,50@50).drawFunc_({val.value(Rect(0,0,50,50))}).background_(Color.grey(0.7));
       	(i%2).booleanValue.if{ w.startRow;};
    };
}
)

::
